{"codeSnippets":[{"codeTitle":"useState(initialState)","codeDescription":"Calls useState at the top level of a component to declare a state variable. Returns a pair with the current state value and a setter function to trigger re-renders.","codeLanguage":"APIDOC","codeTokens":221,"codeId":"https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/reference/react/useState.md","pageTitle":"Unknown","codeList":[{"language":"APIDOC","code":"## useState(initialState)\n\n### Description\nCall `useState` at the top level of your component to declare one or more state variables.\n\n### Parameters\n- **initialState** (any) - The initial value of the state variable.\n\n### Return Value\nReturns an array containing exactly two items:\n1. **currentState** (any) - The current state value, initially set to the `initialState` provided.\n2. **setFunction** (Function) - The `set` function that lets you update the state to any other value and trigger a re-render.\n\n### Example\n```js\nimport { useState } from 'react';\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const [age, setAge] = useState(42);\n  const [name, setName] = useState('Taylor');\n\n  function handleClick() {\n    setName('Robin');\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```"}],"generationDate":"2026-09-11T15:11:49.372Z","rank":1},{"codeTitle":"Declare state variables with useState","codeDescription":"Call useState at the top level of a component to declare state variables. By convention, use array destructuring to get the current state and its matching set function.","codeLanguage":"javascript","codeTokens":84,"codeId":"https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/reference/react/useState.md","pageTitle":"Unknown","codeList":[{"language":"javascript","code":"import { useState } from 'react';\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const [age, setAge] = useState(42);\n  const [name, setName] = useState('Taylor');\n  // ..."}],"generationDate":"2026-09-11T15:11:49.372Z","rank":2},{"codeTitle":"Declare state with useState","codeDescription":"Use useState to declare a state variable that can be updated directly, allowing the component to retain values across renders.","codeLanguage":"javascript","codeTokens":53,"codeId":"https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/reference/react/hooks.md","pageTitle":"Unknown","codeList":[{"language":"javascript","code":"function ImageGallery() {\n  const [index, setIndex] = useState(0);\n  // ..."}],"generationDate":"2026-09-11T14:01:45.667Z","rank":3},{"codeTitle":"Declare state variables with useState","codeDescription":"Call useState with an initial state value to declare state variables and obtain setter functions to update them.","codeLanguage":"javascript","codeTokens":54,"codeId":"https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/learn/adding-interactivity.md","pageTitle":"Unknown","codeList":[{"language":"javascript","code":"const [index, setIndex] = useState(0);\nconst [showMore, setShowMore] = useState(false);"}],"generationDate":"2026-09-11T12:25:40.263Z","rank":4},{"codeTitle":"Declare state variable and setter with useState","codeDescription":"Destructure the state variable snapshot and its corresponding update function returned by the useState Hook.","codeLanguage":"javascript","codeTokens":43,"codeId":"https://github.com/reactjs/react.dev/blob/main/src/content/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure.md","pageTitle":"Unknown","codeList":[{"language":"javascript","code":"const [stateVariable, setter] = useState(0);"}],"generationDate":"2026-09-11T15:48:11.665Z","rank":5}],"infoSnippets":[]}